            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can use this idea to calculate products involving powers of ten in exponent form.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can use this idea to calculate products involving powers of ten in exponent form.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To illustrate, let&#x27;s work out how to compute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6 \\times 10^2.]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "To illustrate, let's work out how to compute [MATH: 6 \\times 10^2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we can expand <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10^2]</span> by writing it as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> followed by a block of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> zeros:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we can expand [MATH: 10^2] by writing it as [MATH: 1] followed by a block of [MATH: 2] zeros:\n[MATH: 2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, to find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6 \\times 100,]</span> we join <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6]</span> with the block of zeros:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, to find [MATH: 6 \\times 100,] we join [MATH: 6] with the block of zeros:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6 \\times 1{\\color{blue}00} =6 {\\color{blue}{00}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 6 \\times 1{\\color{blue}00} =6 {\\color{blue}{00}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6 \\times 10^2 = 600.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, [MATH: 6 \\times 10^2 = 600.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWhen a power of ten is written in exponent form, we can express it as a [MATH: 1] followed by a block of zeros. The number of zeros in the block should equal the exponent. For example,\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2]\n\nContent:\nWe can use this idea to calculate products involving powers of ten in exponent form.\n\nContent:\nTo illustrate, let's work out how to compute [MATH: 6 \\times 10^2.]\n\nContent:\nFirst, we can expand [MATH: 10^2] by writing it as [MATH: 1] followed by a block of [MATH: 2] zeros:\n[MATH: 2]\n\nContent:\nNow, to find [MATH: 6 \\times 100,] we join [MATH: 6] with the block of zeros:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 6 \\times 1{\\color{blue}00} =6 {\\color{blue}{00}}]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: 6 \\times 10^2 = 600.]"
      },
