          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we can expand <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10^1]</span> by writing a <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> followed by a block of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> zero: </p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span></p><p>Now, to find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 29 \\times 10,]</span> we join <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\bbox[2pt, lightgray]{29}]</span> with the block of zeros:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 29 \\times 10^1 = 290.]</span></p>",
